<!-- lexitrail#367 (decided 2026-09-05, HCL): STATIC-ONLY INDEXING. This file lists
     ONLY the homepage and the static hsk*.html indexes. The 14 SPA routes it used to
     carry (/about, /wordsets, 12 /game/*) were removed deliberately, NOT by accident:
     robots.txt blocks Googlebot from the CRA bundle, so every SPA route renders as a
     3496-byte shell with zero links. Asserting an unrenderable shell as a canonical
     index target is worse than not listing it.

     🔴 Do NOT "restore" them without re-opening #367. Removing them does not hide them:
     hsk1.html links every /game/*/PRACTICE route and the gloss landers link them too,
     so they stay discoverable through the in-page link graph. The sitemap entry was the
     only thing being dropped, which is what made this cheap.

     Measured 2026-09-05 at the wire: /, /about, /wordsets and /game/1/PRACTICE were all
     3496 B with 0 <a>; hsk1.html was 34917 B with 157 <a>. The static corpus is ~5010
     URLs (4999 word pages + 6 hsk indexes + 5 gloss landers) and none of it depends on
     JS. See ui/src/utils/sitemapStatic.test.js, which pins this. -->
